  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Delhi is experiencing a significant decline in air quality, with recent data from the Central Pollution Control Board indicating the air has reached severe and hazardous classifications. This deterioration follows the Deepavali festival period, which saw heavy smog settle over the capital. While some observers highlight the impact of firecrackers on air quality, others point to pre-existing pollution conditions, such as seasonal stubble burning and existing toxic levels reported prior to the festivities. Discrepancies in data reporting and the integrity of pollution measurements have become points of contention among political figures. In response to the persistent hazardous conditions, the Delhi government has implemented mitigation efforts such as water sprinkling to address the smog. Research continues to analyze how much of the seasonal pollution can be attributed to specific events versus long-term environmental factors affecting the region.",
